.TH ORO-MCP 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:mcp \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:mcp'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Runtime MCP helpers for registering tools/resources and controlling the native HTTP/SSE bridge.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBregisterTool(tool)\fR
Register a tool that can be invoked by MCP clients.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItool\fR (MCPRegisterToolOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<number \\| null>\fR
.TP
\fBunregisterTool(name)\fR
Unregister a tool by name.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR Whether a registered tool was removed.
.TP
\fBlistTools()\fR
List the currently registered tool descriptors.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<MCPToolDescriptor[]>\fR
.TP
\fBregisterResource(resource)\fR
Register a resource that can be read or subscribed to by MCP clients.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIresource\fR (MCPRegisterResourceOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<number \\| null>\fR
.TP
\fBunregisterResource(uri)\fR
Unregister a resource by URI.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIuri\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR Whether a registered resource was removed.
.TP
\fBlistResources()\fR
List the currently registered resource descriptors.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<MCPResourceDescriptor[]>\fR
.TP
\fBinvokeTool(name, args, options)\fR
Invoke a registered tool through the local MCP service.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIargs\fR (Record<string, any>; optional)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (MCPInvocationOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR Whether the invocation was accepted.
.TP
\fBpublishResource(uri, result, options)\fR
Publish an update to active subscriptions for a registered resource.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIuri\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIresult\fR (MCPResourceHandlerResult; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (MCPPublishResourceOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR Whether at least one matching stream received the update.
.TP
\fBsetAuthorizationHandler(handler)\fR
Configure a runtime authorization handler for incoming MCP HTTP requests. Pass a function to enable dynamic authorization or `null`/`undefined` to clear. The handler can return a boolean or an {@link MCPAuthorizationDecision} object.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIhandler\fR ((request: MCPAuthorizationRequest) => boolean \\| MCPAuthorizationDecision \\| Promise<boolean \\| MCPAuthorizationDecision> \\| null \\| undefined; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBstartServer(options)\fR
Start the embedded MCP HTTP/SSE bridge.
.br
\- Supplying `port: 0` binds to an ephemeral port and the resolved value is returned in the result. \- `authorize` registers a dynamic authorization handler for this server.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (MCPStartServerOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<MCPStartServerResult>\fR
.TP
\fBstopServer()\fR
Stop the embedded MCP server.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR Whether the server is stopped.
.TP
\fBserverStatus()\fR
Report whether the embedded MCP server is running.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR
